{"agent":"fx-phase-deps","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_docs_only_exempt` calls `path_in_glob(g, d)` where `g` is an element of `it.globs` (a glob pattern) and `d` is an element of `cfg.gates.doc_globs` (also a glob pattern). `path_in_glob` is the imported alias for `inside`, a predicate that checks whether a concrete path is inside a glob pattern, so this is checking whether the literal glob string `\"docs/**\"` matches the doc-glob string `\"docs/*\"`, not whether every file matched by the task glob is a document. For example, with `[gates].doc_globs = [\"docs/*\"]` and a task with `globs = [\"docs/**\"]` (which also matches code files under subdirectories), the literal string `\"docs/**\"` is matched by `\"docs/*\"` because `*` absorbs the literal `**` component, causing `_docs_only_exempt` to return True and a non-doc-only task to skip inherited phase dependencies. The check must reason about glob language/subset or use a glob-overlap predicate, not `path_in_glob`.","digest":"afa94c4f6817acf2","location":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_docs_only_exempt","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule.py:_docs_only_exempt"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":9499,"diff_sha":"00ba8c1f6328f0c4318f36ace4d89d7f5ac67cd58deb806f35f96e1e7a1bce75","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":549.2,"excluded_bytes":2687,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"6f95a11f08290b32","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-research-task-inherits-phase-deps.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261021T173150Z-f2c4dc15.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"395f0c0c7af01ab1b6c53ec794ad42a7